# Local, machine-specific — never commit

# Local Mac reimage workflow config
reimage.env

# Archived/stale copies from Check for an Existing reimage.env
reimage.env.stale-*

*.local.sh

# Resolved, machine-specific companions to committed docs
# (e.g. post-reimage-cheatsheet.local.md — real paths, asset tag, DMG filename)
*.local.md

# Build artifacts from bin/build-jump-drive-payload.sh
.toolkit-version
*.tar.gz
*.tar.gz.sha256

# macOS / editor noise
.DS_Store
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Obsidian vault config -- local editor state, not shared repo content
.obsidian/

# JetBrains IDEs (IntelliJ IDEA, WebStorm, PyCharm)
# Written as `.idea/*` rather than `.idea/` on purpose: git does not descend into a
# directory excluded wholesale, so a negation like `!.idea/codeStyles/` would be
# ignored. This form leaves the door open.
#
# If the team ever standardizes on IntelliJ, these are the ones worth sharing —
# uncomment to re-include:
#   !.idea/codeStyles/          formatting, so diffs stop churning between developers
#   !.idea/inspectionProfiles/  shared lint expectations
#   !.idea/runConfigurations/   e.g. serve:http, npm test
#   !.idea/vcs.xml              tells IntelliJ the project root is a Git repo; identical for everyone
#
# Never share, whatever the team decides: workspace.xml (per-user UI state, huge and
# constantly dirty), tasks.xml, usage.statistics.xml, shelf/, httpRequests/ (scratch
# requests can hold live tokens), dataSources.xml + dataSources.local.xml (connection
# details, sometimes credentials), and *.iml (absolute machine paths).
.idea/*
*.iml
*.ipr
*.iws
/out/

